  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Combating food insecurity among the most vulnerable groups in South Sudan</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The project scope is to support small scale food producers increase their capacity to adopt climate resilient techniques through equipping them with agricultural tools and inputs and engaging women and youth in income generating activities. Oxfam is going to implement this project with a local partner called Community Initiative for Development Organization (CIDO), a women right organization (WRO) with strong food security and livelihoods expertise and presence in the area of intervention. the project has targeted 21200 vulnerable people in Akobo county.</narrative>
  </description>
